["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Most \"gamey\" deer were ruined in the pan, not the field. Wild meat is lean. Heat is the enemy twice.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 436\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Thermometer chart of cooking temperatures in degrees Celsius. 71: all wild game, ground meat and bear, the Canadian Food Inspection Agency food safety number, 95 percent. 74: game birds, 80 percent. 77: bear per Washington, 80 percent. 60 to 63: deer loin as many hunters cook it, a personal risk and not a safe number. Bear: never pink.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"436\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cooking temperatures, °C</text><rect x=\"58\" y=\"50\" width=\"24\" height=\"340\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"402\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><rect x=\"65\" y=\"92\" width=\"10\" height=\"298\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"380\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"380\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"385.0\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">50</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"327\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"327\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"331.6666666666667\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">55</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"273\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"273\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"278.3333333333333\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">60</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"225.0\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">65</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"167\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"167\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"171.66666666666666\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">70</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"113\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"113\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"118.33333333333331\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">75</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"65.0\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">80</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"112\" y=\"77.0\" width=\"268\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"97.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bear: 77°C per Washington (80%)</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"112\" y=\"109.0\" width=\"268\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"129.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Game birds: 74°C (80%)</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"156\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"156\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"112\" y=\"141.0\" width=\"268\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">All wild game, ground, bear: 71°C</text><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"257\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"257\" stroke=\"#7a7a7a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"112\" y=\"242.33333333333331\" width=\"268\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#7a7a7a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"262.3333333333333\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#7a7a7a\" text-anchor=\"start\">Deer loin, 60 to 63°C: many hunters</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"188.0\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Canadian food safety number (95%)</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"289.3333333333333\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7a7a7a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your risk, not a safe number. Lean.</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"307.3333333333333\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b3261e\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear: never.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>71°C is Canada's food safety number for all wild game <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Bear and ground meat: 71°C, no debate <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: lean meat and the safety number</summary><ul><li>Deer, moose and elk have almost no fat inside the muscle. Overcooked, they turn grey and dry (80%, North Dakota State University: venison steak 1.4% fat).</li><li>Food safety says 71°C internal for all wild game (95%, Canadian Food Inspection Agency). Hunters often eat deer steaks pinker. That is a personal risk call, labelled below.</li><li>Bear and ground meat: 71°C, no debate <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 378\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Deer cut chart coloured by cooking method. Orange, hot pan and short time: backstrap, tenderloin and hind leg steaks; hind leg roasts go in the oven. Brown, low and slow for 2.5 to 3 hours: neck, shoulder and shank braised, ribs smoked or braised.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"378\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fast cuts, slow cuts</text><g transform=\"translate(0 30)\"><polygon points=\"170,196 190,196 186,272 176,272\" fill=\"#e8e2d4\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#b9b09d\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"272,200 292,200 286,272 278,272\" fill=\"#e8e2d4\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#b9b09d\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"78,64 100,56 152,106 150,152 126,160 100,104\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"152,106 172,108 172,126 205,128 205,160 180,198 150,200 126,160 150,152\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"172,108 230,108 300,106 300,126 205,128 172,126\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"205,128 268,127 262,193 180,198 205,160\" fill=\"#a0643a\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"268,127 300,126 300,106 320,110 336,140 330,180 316,206 290,206 262,193\" fill=\"#f08c4a\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"138,199 164,199 160,236 142,236\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"142,236 160,236 156,272 146,272\" fill=\"#e8e2d4\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"290,206 316,206 312,240 294,240\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"294,240 312,240 310,272 300,272\" fill=\"#e8e2d4\" fill-opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M100 56 Q86 50 70 58 Q54 66 50 74 Q54 81 66 80 Q82 78 96 72 Z\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><path d=\"M96 56 L104 38 L108 60 Z\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"74\" cy=\"66\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"276\" cy=\"136\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#b3261e\" fill-opacity=\".85\" stroke=\"#b3261e\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"236\" y1=\"117\" x2=\"274\" y2=\"71\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><circle cx=\"236\" cy=\"117\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">Backstrap: hot, fast</text><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"288\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><circle cx=\"312\" cy=\"160\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"307\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0601c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Leg: steaks or roast</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"137\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"170\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"8\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shoulder: braise</text><line x1=\"116\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"106\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"8\" y=\"145\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Neck: braise</text><line x1=\"232\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"288\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><circle cx=\"232\" cy=\"170\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"307\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ribs: smoke</text></g><rect x=\"30\" y=\"350\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"362\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hot pan, short time</text><rect x=\"210\" y=\"350\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"232\" y=\"362\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Low and slow, 2.5 to 3 h</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Tender cuts: hot and fast. Tough cuts: low and slow (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full table by cut</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Cut</th><th>Method</th><th>Done when</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tenderloin, backstrap</td><td>Hot pan or grill, fast, then rest</td><td>Medium rare to medium is common hunter practice (Tip); 71°C is the food safety number <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Hind leg steaks</td><td>Hot and fast, or marinate first</td><td>Same</td></tr><tr><td>Hind leg roasts</td><td>Oven at 160°C, or sear then low</td><td>Same, rest 10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Shoulder, neck, shank</td><td>Braise or stew, 2.5 to 3 hours with liquid</td><td>Falls apart</td></tr><tr><td>Ribs</td><td>Slow smoke or braise</td><td>Falls off the bone</td></tr><tr><td>Ground</td><td>Burgers, chili, sausage</td><td>71°C (160°F), no pink <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Bear, any cut</td><td>Roast, braise, or stew</td><td>71°C minimum everywhere in the cut <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Game birds</td><td>Roast whole plucked, or pan fry breasts</td><td>74°C (165°F) (80%, North Dakota State University)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Old or stiff jointed bird: braise or stew it (80%, North Dakota State University).</li><li>A rutting buck or an old bull: braise and stew more, steak less. Tip.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 310\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, a tip: a steak in a hot pan. The thermometer climbs to 5 degrees below the target, then you pull it off the heat and rest it 5 minutes while it climbs the last few degrees. Ground meat and bear still need 71 degrees.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pull early, then rest (Tip)</text><g transform=\"translate(110 150) scale(3.0)\"><ellipse cx=\"-4\" cy=\"4\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M12 2 L24 -2\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-10 -6 q3 -5 0 -10 M-3 -6 q3 -5 0 -10 M4 -6 q3 -5 0 -10\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/></g><rect x=\"268\" y=\"60\" width=\"26\" height=\"180\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"281\" cy=\"250\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"230\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#b3261e\"><animate attributeName=\"y\" values=\"230;120;120;100\" keyTimes=\"0;.5;.7;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"height\" values=\"10;120;120;140\" keyTimes=\"0;.5;.7;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></rect><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"334\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">Target</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"334\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">5° less</text><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"236\" width=\"210\" height=\"30\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pull it off the heat</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"272\" width=\"210\" height=\"30\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rest 5 minutes</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Pull 5°C early, rest 5 minutes. Tip. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Use a probe thermometer. Grey means dry (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full list and my lean</summary><ul><li>Lean muscle has no fat to carry it past medium. Grey means dry and livery. Tip.</li><li>Use a probe thermometer. Pull steaks 5°C before the target and rest them 5 minutes. Tip.</li><li>Thin steaks: 2 to 3 minutes a side in a smoking hot pan. Tip.</li><li>Low and slow is for the tough cuts, not the loin. Tip.</li><li>Food safety sources say all game to 71°C or more (95%, Canadian Food Inspection Agency), 74°C per Washington <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Nobody says rare is safe. My lean: deer loin at 60°C to 63°C is what most hunters do, and the risk is theirs. Bear never.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 312\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bear meat safety. Freezing, curing or salting, drying, smoking and microwaving do not reliably kill Trichinella larvae, 95 percent. Only heat does: cook to 71 degrees Celsius or more in the thickest part of every piece. No pink bear, ever.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"312\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear: only heat makes it safe</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"46\" width=\"88\" height=\"112\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fdf0e6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(54 86) scale(1.1)\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"18.0\" y2=\"0.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"9.0\" y2=\"15.6\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-9.0\" y2=\"15.6\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-18.0\" y2=\"0.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-9.0\" y2=\"-15.6\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"9.0\" y2=\"-15.6\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><circle cx=\"84\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M79 55 l10 10 M89 55 l-10 10\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Freezing</text><rect x=\"106\" y=\"46\" width=\"88\" height=\"112\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fdf0e6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(150 86) scale(1.1)\"><path d=\"M-10 -8 h20 l3 26 h-26 z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-10 -8 q10 -14 20 0\" fill=\"#cfd6bf\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"-3\" cy=\"-11\" r=\"1.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"3\" cy=\"-11\" r=\"1.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M175 55 l10 10 M185 55 l-10 10\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Curing,</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"151\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">salting</text><rect x=\"202\" y=\"46\" width=\"88\" height=\"112\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fdf0e6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(246 86) scale(1.1)\"><circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"13.0\" y1=\"0.0\" x2=\"19.0\" y2=\"0.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"9.2\" y1=\"9.2\" x2=\"13.4\" y2=\"13.4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"0.0\" y1=\"13.0\" x2=\"0.0\" y2=\"19.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-9.2\" y1=\"9.2\" x2=\"-13.4\" y2=\"13.4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-13.0\" y1=\"0.0\" x2=\"-19.0\" y2=\"0.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-9.2\" y1=\"-9.2\" x2=\"-13.4\" y2=\"-13.4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-0.0\" y1=\"-13.0\" x2=\"-0.0\" y2=\"-19.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"9.2\" y1=\"-9.2\" x2=\"13.4\" y2=\"-13.4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><circle cx=\"276\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M271 55 l10 10 M281 55 l-10 10\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"246\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Drying</text><rect x=\"298\" y=\"46\" width=\"88\" height=\"112\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fdf0e6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(342 86) scale(1.1)\"><path d=\"M0 -18 C10 -6 14 2 8 12 C4 18 -6 18 -9 10 C-12 2 -4 -2 0 -18 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M-14 16 L14 10 M-14 10 L14 16\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M367 55 l10 10 M377 55 l-10 10\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"342\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Smoking</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nor microwaving. None of these reliably</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">kill Trichinella larvae (95%)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"208\" width=\"380\" height=\"92\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f3f6ec\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><g transform=\"translate(50 254) scale(1.5)\"><rect x=\"-5\" y=\"-20\" width=\"10\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"-2\" y=\"-6\" width=\"4\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/></g><text x=\"90\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Cook to 71°C or more</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">in the thickest part, every piece</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b3261e\" text-anchor=\"start\">No pink bear. Ever.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Frozen bear is still raw bear <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the food safety words and symptoms</summary><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">The rule</div><p>Food safety advice, not a hunting rule: \"All wild game meat, pork and horse meat should be cooked to an internal temperature of at least 71°C. Curing (salting), drying, smoking or microwaving the meat does not consistently kill infective larvae\" (95%, Canadian Food Inspection Agency).</p></aside><ul><li>Bears carry Trichinella. In Canada \"the primary risk\" of trichinellosis is \"undercooked or raw meat from wildlife species such as bears and walruses\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>\"Most species of Trichinella found in wildlife are resistant to freezing\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Frozen bear is still raw bear.</li><li>Thermometer in the thickest part. 71°C or more, every piece. Washington says 77°C (170°F) for bear <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>No bear jerky, no bear sausage eaten uncooked, no pink bear burgers <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Symptoms 5 to 15 days after eating: fever, facial swelling, muscle pain, rash. See a doctor and say \"bear meat\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 350\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Plucking or breasting birds. Pluck: the skin keeps flavour and moisture, roast whole ducks plucked, 80 percent. Breast out: fast and fine for grouse and quail in a pan, a tip. Law: both breasts are the legal minimum you must keep from any game bird. Cook bird meat to 74 degrees Celsius, 80 percent.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"350\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Birds: pluck or breast?</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"185\" height=\"142\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(40 78) scale(0.9)\"><path d=\"M-14 18 Q-8 -8 14 -18 Q8 4 -14 18 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-14 18 L6 -8\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></g><text x=\"68\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Pluck</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Skin keeps</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">flavour and</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">moisture. Roast</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">whole ducks</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">(80%)</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"44\" width=\"185\" height=\"142\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(235 78) scale(0.9)\"><path d=\"M-20 6 L6 -4 Q16 -8 20 -12 Q18 2 6 6 Z\" fill=\"#cfd6bf\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"-24\" y=\"2\" width=\"14\" height=\"9\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" transform=\"rotate(-20 -17 6)\"/></g><text x=\"263\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Breast out</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Fast. Fine for</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">grouse and quail</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">in a pan (Tip)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"196\" width=\"185\" height=\"142\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(40 230) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"4\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M17 -6 l6 1 l-6 2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M-4 2 Q-14 -14 4 -6\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><rect x=\"141\" y=\"314\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"165\" y=\"329\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">LAW</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Keep both</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">breasts</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">The legal</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">minimum from any</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">game bird (95%)</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"196\" width=\"185\" height=\"142\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(235 230) scale(0.9)\"><rect x=\"-5\" y=\"-20\" width=\"10\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"-2\" y=\"-6\" width=\"4\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/></g><text x=\"263\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bird meat 74°C</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">North Dakota</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">State University</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">(80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Roast ducks whole and plucked. Pan fry grouse breasts (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: plucking and breasting in full</summary><ul><li>Plucking keeps the skin. \"The skin helps retain flavor and moisture during cooking\" (80%, Penn State Extension). Roast whole ducks plucked.</li><li>Pluck a few feathers at a time. Dry pluck, then paraffin and hot water for the down (80%, North Dakota State University).</li><li>Breasting: peel the skin, cut the breasts off the keel. Fast, and fine for grouse and quail in a pan (Tip).</li><li>The legal minimum you must keep from any game bird is \"both breasts\" (95%, synopsis p. 3). The legs are a bonus. Tip.</li><li>Bird meat to 74°C (165°F) (80%, North Dakota State University).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 296\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two birds. Grouse and quail, and other non migratory game birds: one feathered wing stays attached. Ducks and geese, and other migratory game birds: one feathered wing or the feathered head stays attached. A turkey from a bearded turkey only season also keeps the beard.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"296\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Birds: what stays attached</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"42\" width=\"188\" height=\"210\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(100 110) scale(2.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M19 -10 L24 -9 L19 -7 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-14 -4 L-28 -12 L-28 4 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-2 10 L-2 18 M4 10 L4 18\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"104\" r=\"24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse, quail:</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">one feathered</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">wing</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"42\" width=\"188\" height=\"210\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(296 110) scale(2.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"15\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2e6b3a\"/><path d=\"M21 -9 L29 -7 L21 -5 Z\" fill=\"#e0a526\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-26 -6 L-22 2 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"90\" r=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<circle cx=\"280\" cy=\"108\" r=\"22\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ducks, geese:</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">one feathered wing</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">OR the feathered head</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Turkey, bearded only season: the beard too.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>The feathered wing stays on until the bird is home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the rule in full</summary><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">The rule</div><p>Grouse and quail: \"must leave attached to the carcass one feathered wing\". Ducks and geese: \"one feathered wing or the feathered head\" (95%, synopsis p. 15).</p></aside><ul><li>The wing stays on until the bird is home. Breast it out in the field if you like, but leave one feathered wing on the piece you keep <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>It lets an officer count and identify species in your cooler (Tip, the reason behind the rule).</li><li>Possession limit for ducks is three times the daily limit, including at home (95%, p. 12).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Backstrap in the pan</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Backstrap in the pan, step 1: Dry it, salt it. Pat the meat dry. Salt both sides. Recipe, a tip.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".35\"/><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"32\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"37\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dry it, salt it</text><g transform=\"translate(200 140) scale(3.0)\"><path d=\"M-10 -8 h20 l3 26 h-26 z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-10 -8 q10 -14 20 0\" fill=\"#cfd6bf\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"-3\" cy=\"-11\" r=\"1.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"3\" cy=\"-11\" r=\"1.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><rect x=\"250\" y=\"150\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#c0504d\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pat the meat dry. Salt both sides.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Recipe: Tip.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Dry the meat. Salt it.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Backstrap in the pan, step 2: Smoking hot pan. Cast iron, a little oil. 2 to 3 min a side, 3 cm piece. Recipe, a tip.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".35\"/><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"32\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"37\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Smoking hot pan</text><g transform=\"translate(200 140) scale(3.0)\"><ellipse cx=\"-4\" cy=\"4\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M12 2 L24 -2\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-10 -6 q3 -5 0 -10 M-3 -6 q3 -5 0 -10 M4 -6 q3 -5 0 -10\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cast iron, a little oil. 2 to 3 min a</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">side, 3 cm piece.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Recipe: Tip.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Smoking hot cast iron. 2 to 3 minutes a side.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Backstrap in the pan, step 3: Butter, garlic. Add butter and garlic in the last minute. Recipe, a tip.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".35\"/><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"32\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"37\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Butter, garlic</text><g transform=\"translate(200 140) scale(3.0)\"><ellipse cx=\"-4\" cy=\"4\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M12 2 L24 -2\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-10 -6 q3 -5 0 -10 M-3 -6 q3 -5 0 -10 M4 -6 q3 -5 0 -10\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/></g><rect x=\"150\" y=\"118\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"124\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#f5f0e0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Add butter and garlic in the last minute.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Recipe: Tip.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Butter and garlic in the last minute.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Backstrap in the pan, step 4: Rest, then slice. Rest 5 minutes. Slice across the grain. Recipe, a tip.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".35\"/><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"32\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"37\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rest, then slice</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"110\" width=\"30\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0504d\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"116\" y=\"120\" width=\"18\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8a0a0\"/><rect x=\"146\" y=\"110\" width=\"30\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0504d\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"152\" y=\"120\" width=\"18\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8a0a0\"/><rect x=\"182\" y=\"110\" width=\"30\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0504d\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"188\" y=\"120\" width=\"18\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8a0a0\"/><rect x=\"218\" y=\"110\" width=\"30\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0504d\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"224\" y=\"120\" width=\"18\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8a0a0\"/><rect x=\"254\" y=\"110\" width=\"30\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0504d\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"260\" y=\"120\" width=\"18\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8a0a0\"/><g transform=\"translate(330 100) scale(1.4)\"><path d=\"M-20 6 L6 -4 Q16 -8 20 -12 Q18 2 6 6 Z\" fill=\"#cfd6bf\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"-24\" y=\"2\" width=\"14\" height=\"9\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" transform=\"rotate(-20 -17 6)\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rest 5 minutes. Slice across the grain.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Recipe: Tip.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Rest 5 minutes. Slice across the grain.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Two more below: shoulder stew and grouse breasts (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all three recipes in full</summary><ol><li>Backstrap in the pan. Dry the meat. Salt. Cast iron, smoking hot, a little oil. 2 to 3 minutes a side for a 3 cm piece. Butter and garlic in the last minute. Rest 5 minutes. Slice across the grain. Tip.</li><li>Shoulder stew. Cube the shoulder and neck, flour and salt them, brown in batches. Onion, carrot, garlic, a tin of tomatoes, stock to cover, bay leaf. Lid on, oven at 150°C for 3 hours. Tip. The North Dakota State University version simmers 45 minutes for small strips <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Grouse breasts. Flour, salt, pepper. Butter in a medium hot pan. 2 to 3 minutes a side until 74°C. Squeeze of lemon. Tip. A whole plucked duck instead: apples in the cavity, roast at 160°C (325°F) for 1 to 1.5 hours, basting (80%, North Dakota State University).</li></ol></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 336\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Where a gamey taste comes from: poor bleeding, slow or careless dressing, slow cooling, fat and silver skin left on, hair, gut contents or a warm truck, and sometimes a rutting buck, which you braise. Myth: soak it in milk. Clean, cool, well trimmed meat needs no soak.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"336\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Where &quot;gamey&quot; really comes from</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(40 78) scale(0.9)\"><path d=\"M-14 -18 H8 L16 -10 V18 H-14 Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-8 -6 H10 M-8 2 H10 M-8 10 H4\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g><text x=\"68\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Poor bleeding</text><rect x=\"203\" y=\"44\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(233 78) scale(0.9)\"><path d=\"M-20 6 L6 -4 Q16 -8 20 -12 Q18 2 6 6 Z\" fill=\"#cfd6bf\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"-24\" y=\"2\" width=\"14\" height=\"9\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" transform=\"rotate(-20 -17 6)\"/></g><text x=\"261\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Slow or</text><text x=\"261\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">careless</text><text x=\"261\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">dressing</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(40 156) scale(0.9)\"><rect x=\"-5\" y=\"-20\" width=\"10\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"-2\" y=\"-6\" width=\"4\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/></g><text x=\"68\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Slow cooling</text><rect x=\"203\" y=\"122\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(233 156) scale(0.9)\"><path d=\"M-18 -4 Q-14 -18 6 -14 Q22 -10 18 6 Q12 18 -6 14 Q-20 10 -18 -4 Z\" fill=\"#c0504d\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-8 -2 Q2 -8 10 0\" stroke=\"#f5e0d8\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#f5f0e0\"/></g><text x=\"261\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Fat and silver</text><text x=\"261\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">skin left on</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"200\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(40 234) scale(0.9)\"><rect x=\"-22\" y=\"-6\" width=\"26\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M4 -2 h10 l6 6 v6 h-16 z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"68\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hair, gut</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">contents, warm</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">truck</text><rect x=\"203\" y=\"200\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(233 234) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse cx=\"2\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-10 8 v12 M-4 8 v12 M8 8 v12 M14 8 v12\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-12 -2 L-18 -12\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"-20\" cy=\"-14\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-19 -18 l-2 -8 m2 4 l4 -5 M-17 -18 l3 -6\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><text x=\"261\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rutting buck:</text><text x=\"261\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">braise it</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"280\" width=\"380\" height=\"46\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fdf0e6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"303\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M29 298 l10 10 M39 298 l-10 10\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"56\" y=\"309\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Myth: soak it in milk. Clean meat needs none.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>\"Gamey\" is mostly handling, not the animal <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the myths and facts in full</summary><ul><li>\"Gamey\" is mostly handling. \"Undesirable strong flavors in the meat can be due to inadequate bleeding, delay or carelessness in dressing or failure to cool the carcass promptly. Occasionally, the diet of the animal will affect the flavor\" (80%, North Dakota State University).</li><li>Myth: soak it in milk. Clean, cool, well trimmed meat needs no soak. Tip.</li><li>Fact: deer fat is waxy. Trim it. Most \"gamey\" burger is fat and silver skin. Tip.</li><li>Fact: hair, gut contents and a warm truck taint meat. Session 8. Tip.</li><li>Fact: a rutting buck can taste stronger. Braise it. Tip.</li><li>Fact: aging at 1°C to 3°C for 7 to 14 days improves tenderness and flavour (80%, Washington Department of Fish and Wildlife).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Hot pan, short time, long rest. Tough cuts get the whole afternoon.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Cooking a backstrap like a pot roast.</li><li>Pink bear steak \"because it was frozen\".</li><li>Breasting out a duck and tossing the wing before you get home.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Tonight's camp meal: the tenderloins, salt, a hot pan, 2 minutes a side. Nothing else.</p></aside>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://inspection.canada.ca/en/animal-health/terrestrial-animals/diseases/reportable/trichinellosis/fact-sheet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Canadian Food Inspection Agency, Trichinellosis fact sheet</a>, read directly, 95%. Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ndsu.edu/agriculture/extension/publications/wild-side-menu-no-1-care-and-cookery\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">North Dakota State University Extension, Wild Side of the Menu No. 1: Care and Cookery</a>, read directly, 80%: temperatures, plucking, flavour causes, duck and venison recipes. Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://extension.psu.edu/proper-field-dressing-and-handling-of-wild-game-and-fish\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Penn State Extension, Proper field dressing and handling of wild game and fish</a>, read directly, 80%. Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/hunting/requirements/food-safety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Washington Department of Fish and Wildlife, food safety guidelines for game meat</a>, read directly, 80%. Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, printed p. 3 (edible portions), p. 12 (possession limits), p. 15 (wing or head). Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li>Recipes and doneness preferences: Tip. The 71°C figure is the only food safety number here that is official for Canada.</li></ul>"]